title: Wire OCP::Hetzner location/server_type pickers into ocp init
updated: 2026-08-15T07:52:02Z
---

OCP::Hetzner::location_options and server_type_options build ready-to-use picker lists (label + value) and still have no callers - grep over lib/ and bin/ finds only their own definitions. ocp init --hetzner prompts for the API token and then writes the hardcoded cpx21/fsn1/debian-13 defaults from OCP::Config::write_spec without ever asking.

Since the token is already in hand at that point in Init.pm step 6, the two lists are exactly what an interactive follow-up prompt needs. Ticket 14 made server_type_options safe for that (both architectures, architecture named in the label, deterministic order), so the remaining work is the prompting and passing server_type/location/image through to write_spec.

Either do that, or delete both methods. Two methods that no code path reaches are the reason the x86 default sat there unnoticed.
